{"analysis":"Version 2 scored 59.2 macro-F1, about the same as version 0 (60.0). Positive recall (250) and negative recall (134) are good, but neutral recall is only 26 of 143. Neutral texts leak almost evenly to positive (60) and negative (57).

The neutral texts labelled negative are mostly:
- deadpan or witty observations with no victim and no annoyance ('Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette... Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor', 'Čovjek hoda po rivi... METNEM. Eto.', 'Kolega... pustio intervju s profesorom');
- calm opinions and analysis on politics or society ('moramo se ugledati u Austriju', 'Srbija: Konvencija o genocidu', 'kritičko razmišljanje... protudržavno');
- statistics;
- casual banter with friends.

The negative texts that version 1 lost were different. They were the poster's own complaints about something bothering them (rain again, flu, mosquitoes, traffic, low pay), sarcasm aimed at a target, and bad-news headlines (debt, GDP fall, conflicts). So the useful line is whether the poster is bothered or attacking something, or just observing or joking.

The neutral texts labelled positive are plain informational shares: cooking facts, horoscopes, religious quotes, product links, workshops, line-ups. Here the gold labels look inconsistent, because similar positive-gold texts exist (Soros, WhatsApp, 'Kako povezati znanost'). I will keep shares positive, except pure facts, quotes and specs with no appeal, which go to neutral.

The flood-help appeals are also mixed between positive and neutral, so they stay positive.

Plan for version 3: refine the boundary between neutral and negative using this bothered-or-attacking test, and keep everything else as in version 2.","question":"What emotional attitude does the poster of this Croatian tweet convey, judged from its tone and from the valence of what it reports or shares?","rule":"Negative needs the poster to be bothered or attacking: their own complaint or suffering, annoyance, sarcasm aimed at a person or thing, or news of a bad event (crisis, debt, conflict, death, scandal), even if mild or with a smiley. Deadpan or witty observations with no target, playful banter, and calmly stated opinions, analysis or statistics are neutral. Shares and announcements of culture, events, entertainment, celebrities, tech, business deals, tips, jobs, products, calls to help, and warm replies are positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Joy, praise, thanks, warmth, greetings, anticipation. Shares and announcements of events, culture, films, celebrities, tech, business deals, articles to read, jobs, products, help or volunteer appeals, nice check-ins.","examples":["Pula: Na Giardinima započela 8. Florija, sajam cvijeća u sklopu obilježavanja Dana Grada: https://t.co/6Jbezcjeer (Pula: the 8th Florija flower fair started at Giardini)","Facebook kupuje WhatsApp - cijena - 16 milijardi USD. http://t.co/hQzOMJraPK (Facebook buys WhatsApp for 16 billion USD)","RT @amaiia_hr: #Zagreb - Volonteri traže prijevoz do poplavljenih područja #poplave (Volunteers seek transport to flooded areas)","@msrsan evo, whatever happens znas da si voljen :P (whatever happens, you know you're loved)"],"cues":"premijera (premiere), festival, pobjeda (win), rekord (record), pročitajte (read), traži (seeks), pomozimo (let's help), hvala (thanks), bravo, kava (coffee), :), :D","not_for":"Smileys on complaints or digs go negative. Bare facts, quotes, line-ups and calm political news go neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Matter-of-fact statements, pure facts, quotes, line-ups and specs. Calm opinions or analysis about politics and society, and statistics. Deadpan or witty everyday observations with no target, and playful banter or questions between friends.","examples":["Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette. Žena gleda američki Masterchef. Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor. (Mom watches German Bachelorette. My wife watches American Masterchef. I'm starting to save for a third TV.)","@AnamariaRadi @IKopric definitivno;mislim da se moramo ugledati u Austriju ili Njemacku,ali nas koci financijska situacija,ali  i mentalitet (definitely; I think we should follow Austria or Germany, but finances and mentality hold us back)","RT @321Kuhaj: Divljač se briše papirom, ne pere se vodom. #321kuhaj (Game meat is wiped with paper, not washed with water.)"],"cues":"plain questions, numbers, line-ups, 'Eto' (there you go), 'mislim da' (I think), haha banter, quotes","not_for":"The poster's own annoyance, or bad-news headlines, go negative. Shares inviting readers to events or content go positive."},"negative":{"what":"The poster complains, suffers, is annoyed, sad or worried, insults or mocks someone, or uses sarcasm with a target. Also news of bad events: crises, debt, recession, conflicts, deaths, scandals, failures.","examples":["Naravno, opet kiša u Brusselsu. (Of course, rain in Brussels again.)","Oborili sve rekorde: vanjski dug Hrvatske veći nego ikad http://t.co/YXbdqvWN4o (Broke all records: Croatia's foreign debt higher than ever)","@LucijaCavric oho i ovdje si finjak :P (oho, you're being posh here too)"],"cues":"opet (again), jebiga (damn it), mrzim (I hate), sranje (crap), grozan (awful), gripa (flu), pad (fall), dug (debt), skandal (scandal), napetosti (tensions), :(, :S","not_for":"Help appeals go positive. Witty observations with no target and calm opinions go neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 3 is the best so far at 62.8 macro-F1. Neutral recall rose to 45 of 143, but 60 neutral texts still go to positive.

Those neutral texts labelled positive are mostly of five kinds:
- political and institutional events (EU debate, parliament session, an MP meeting citizens, an association's proposals, EU measures);
- product listings or specs with no praise (Dynaudio SUB, beer, art piece);
- horoscopes, religious quotes and Bible readings;
- practical help or instruction replies in chat;
- course or application notices.

Positive-gold shares are mostly culture, entertainment, celebrity, sport, tech or business-success content, or articles framed as interesting reads. So I will add an explicit neutral bucket: political or institutional events and debates, religious or horoscope texts, bare product names or specs, and practical how-to replies.

The negative texts labelled neutral (25) are mostly self-mocking reports of the poster's own small mishaps (eye bags, torn sneakers, effort removing nail polish) and moralising remarks. I will add the poster's own mishaps, even when joking, to negative.

I keep the rest of version 3 unchanged and stay under 400 words.","question":"What emotional attitude does the poster of this Croatian tweet convey, judged from its tone and from the valence of what it reports or shares?","rule":"Negative needs the poster to be bothered or attacking: their own complaint, mishap or suffering (even joked about), annoyance, sarcasm aimed at someone, moralising criticism, or news of a bad event (crisis, debt, conflict, death, scandal). Deadpan observations about others, banter, calm opinions, statistics, political or institutional events, religious or horoscope texts, bare product specs and practical how-to replies are neutral. Shares of culture, entertainment, celebrities, sport, tech, business deals, interesting articles, jobs, calls to help, and warm replies are positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Joy, praise, thanks, warmth, anticipation. Shares of events, culture, celebrities, sport, tech, business deals, interesting articles, jobs, help appeals, nice check-ins.","examples":["Pula: Na Giardinima započela 8. Florija, sajam cvijeća u sklopu obilježavanja Dana Grada: https://t.co/6Jbezcjeer (Pula: the 8th Florija flower fair started at Giardini)","Facebook kupuje WhatsApp - cijena - 16 milijardi USD. http://t.co/hQzOMJraPK (Facebook buys WhatsApp for 16 billion USD)","RT @amaiia_hr: #Zagreb - Volonteri traže prijevoz do poplavljenih područja #poplave (Volunteers seek transport to flooded areas)"],"cues":"premijera (premiere), festival, pobjeda (win), rekord (record), pročitajte (read), pomozimo (let's help), hvala (thanks), bravo, :), :D","not_for":"Smileys on complaints or digs go negative. Political events, religious texts, horoscopes, specs and instructions go neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Pure facts, quotes, line-ups, statistics, product names or specs. Political or institutional events, debates and calm opinions. Religious texts, horoscopes. Practical how-to replies, banter, and deadpan observations about others.","examples":["Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette. Žena gleda američki Masterchef. Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor. (Mom watches German Bachelorette. My wife watches American Masterchef. I'm starting to save for a third TV.)","Ne propustite večeras debatu kandidata za predsjednika @EU_Commission @hrtvijesti http://t.co/EgGMQ2dir7 (Don't miss tonight's debate of candidates for Commission president)","RT @321Kuhaj: Divljač se briše papirom, ne pere se vodom. #321kuhaj (Game meat is wiped with paper, not washed with water.)"],"cues":"sabor (parliament), zastupnik (MP), sjednica (session), debata (debate), horoskop, Evanđelje (Gospel), plain questions, numbers, 'mislim da' (I think), haha","not_for":"The poster's own annoyance or mishap, or bad-news headlines, go negative. Culture or entertainment shares go positive."},"negative":{"what":"The poster complains, suffers a mishap, is annoyed, sad or worried, insults, mocks or moralises. Also news of bad events: crises, debt, conflicts, deaths, scandals, failures.","examples":["Naravno, opet kiša u Brusselsu. (Of course, rain in Brussels again.)","Oborili sve rekorde: vanjski dug Hrvatske veći nego ikad http://t.co/YXbdqvWN4o (Broke all records: Croatia's foreign debt higher than ever)","@LucijaCavric oho i ovdje si finjak :P (oho, you're being posh here too)"],"cues":"opet (again), jebiga (damn it), mrzim (I hate), sranje (crap), grozan (awful), gripa (flu), dug (debt), skandal (scandal), :(, :S","not_for":"Help appeals go positive. Witty observations about others and calm opinions go neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 6 reached 65.1 macro-F1. Neutral recall rose to 63, but positive texts labelled neutral jumped from 22 to 47.

The new positive-to-neutral errors are friendly @replies and short posts:
- invitations ('popit cemo kavu', 'kad idemo u kazalište?! :D');
- agreement and encouragement ('u pravu si :)', 'Bit će bolje, mora :)', 'nije loše ;)', 'zasluzeno');
- cheering ('ajmo Dinamo', 'Pričekaj Chelsea veceras');
- greetings ('dobar dan :)', 'pozdrav prijatelju');
- playful :D jokes.

The neutral-gold replies that version 6 fixed were mostly informational or logistical answers (settings instructions, TV schedule, 'spreman sam za sjeverni', 'kakvi su dojmovi?').

So I split @replies by their main content:
- positive if the reply is upbeat or friendly: invitation, agreement, encouragement, compliment, greeting, cheering or playful laughter;
- neutral if it mainly gives information, logistics, a question or an opinion, even with a smiley.

I also add article-teaser questions ('Pitanje za milijun dolara!') as a positive cue. Negative stays unchanged.","question":"What emotional attitude does the poster of this Croatian tweet convey, judged from its tone and from the valence of what it reports or shares?","rule":"Negative needs the poster to be bothered or attacking: their own complaint, mishap or suffering (even joked about), annoyance, sarcasm aimed at someone, moralising, or news of something bad (crisis, conflict, criticism, accusation, lawsuit, death, scandal). Replies that mainly give information, logistics, questions or opinions are neutral even with a smiley, as are statistics, deadpan observations, political or institutional events, religious texts and horoscopes. Friendly replies (invitations, agreement, encouragement, greetings, cheering, playful laughter) and shares of culture, entertainment, tech, business deals, teasers, tips, ads, check-ins and help appeals are positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Joy, praise, thanks, warmth, cheering, greetings, invitations, encouragement. Shares of events, culture, celebrities, tech, business deals, article teasers, recipes, ads and listings, check-ins, help appeals.","examples":["Pula: Na Giardinima započela 8. Florija, sajam cvijeća u sklopu obilježavanja Dana Grada: https://t.co/6Jbezcjeer (Pula: the 8th Florija flower fair started at Giardini)","@Kjukar   Ako bude kakve srece, popit cemo kavu negdje ovih dana (If we're lucky, we'll have coffee one of these days)","@sasabca Bit će bolje, mora :) (It will get better, it has to :))","Pitanje za milijun dolara! http://t.co/5gy6q2WrB9 (The million-dollar question!)"],"cues":"festival, ponuda (offer), pročitajte (read), pomozimo (let's help), hvala (thanks), u pravu si (you're right), ajmo (let's go), dobar dan (good day), kava (coffee), :D","not_for":"Smileys on complaints or digs go negative. Informational or logistical replies with a smiley go neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Replies giving information, logistics, plain questions or opinions. Statistics, dividends, line-ups. Political or institutional events and calm opinions. Religious texts, horoscopes. Deadpan observations about others.","examples":["@ewanblaskowicz Nema na čemu. :) Mijenjaš u Postavkama (a gdje drugdje), jezik+regija, promijeniš 'Država/regija' u što hoćeš i restart . (You're welcome :) You change it in Settings, language+region, then restart.)","Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette. Žena gleda američki Masterchef. Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor. (Mom watches German Bachelorette. My wife watches American Masterchef. I'm starting to save for a third TV.)","Ne propustite večeras debatu kandidata za predsjednika @EU_Commission @hrtvijesti http://t.co/EgGMQ2dir7 (Don't miss tonight's debate of candidates for Commission president)"],"cues":"sabor (parliament), debata (debate), dividenda (dividend), horoskop, numbers, instructions, 'mislim da' (I think)","not_for":"The poster's own annoyance or mishap, or bad news, go negative. Friendly or cheering replies and promotional shares go positive."},"negative":{"what":"The poster complains, suffers a mishap, is annoyed, sad or worried, insults, mocks or moralises. Also news of bad things: crises, debt, conflicts, harsh criticism, accusations, lawsuits, deaths, mourning, scandals.","examples":["Naravno, opet kiša u Brusselsu. (Of course, rain in Brussels again.)","Putin na presici žestoko kritizira novo ukrajinsko vodstvo: 'Vojna akcija protiv Ukrajine će biti posljednja opcija!' (Putin harshly criticizes the new Ukrainian leadership)","@LucijaCavric oho i ovdje si finjak :P (oho, you're being posh here too)"],"cues":"opet (again), jebiga (damn it), mrzim (I hate), sranje (crap), grozan (awful), kritizira (criticizes), žalost (mourning), dug (debt), :(, :S","not_for":"Help appeals go positive. Witty observations about others and calm opinions go neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Versions 5 to 8 all score 63 to 65 macro-F1. Version 6 is the best at 65.1, and the differences between versions are largely within noise. Many of the remaining errors are inconsistent gold labels: near-identical friendly replies, flood-help posts, check-ins and cooking tips carry different labels.

Version 8's 'good news is positive' clause pushed borderline neutral news ('Novi zakon prihvatljiv LGBT', 'Drogba... pobjednike') to positive. It also failed to rescue most of the target texts, so the net effect was negative.

Version 9 therefore goes back to version 6, with one small cue change. I swap two weak positive cues for 'kako' (how to) and 'rekord' (record), so how-to teasers and record news lean positive.

Everything else stays as in version 6:
- the rule that a smiley alone does not make an @reply positive;
- the neutral bucket for political events, statistics, religious texts and horoscopes;
- the negative definition built on the poster being bothered or attacking.","question":"What emotional attitude does the poster of this Croatian tweet convey, judged from its tone and from the valence of what it reports or shares?","rule":"Negative needs the poster to be bothered or attacking: their own complaint, mishap or suffering (even joked about), annoyance, sarcasm aimed at someone, moralising, or news of something bad (crisis, conflict, criticism, accusation, lawsuit, death, scandal). Conversational @replies, banter, deadpan observations, calm opinions, statistics, political or institutional events, religious texts and horoscopes are neutral; a smiley alone does not make a reply positive. Shares of culture, entertainment, celebrities, tech, business deals, article teasers, tips, ads, listings, check-ins, help appeals, and replies with explicit warmth are positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit joy, praise, thanks, love, excitement. Shares of events, culture, celebrities, tech, business deals, article teasers, recipes and tips, ads and listings, check-ins, help appeals.","examples":["Pula: Na Giardinima započela 8. Florija, sajam cvijeća u sklopu obilježavanja Dana Grada: https://t.co/6Jbezcjeer (Pula: the 8th Florija flower fair started at Giardini)","Apartments Batur - Zadar - Croatia http://t.co/vLFrL36bKd http://t.co/05CLYU5jQL #croatia","RT @amaiia_hr: #Zagreb - Volonteri traže prijevoz do poplavljenih područja #poplave (Volunteers seek transport to flooded areas)","@msrsan evo, whatever happens znas da si voljen :P (whatever happens, you know you're loved)"],"cues":"festival, ponuda (offer), kako (how to), rekord (record), pročitajte (read), pomozimo (let's help), hvala (thanks), volim (I love), I'm at","not_for":"Smileys on complaints or digs go negative. Casual @reply chat with only a smiley goes neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Casual @reply chat, banter, practical answers, plain questions. Statistics, dividends, line-ups, fan chants. Political or institutional events and calm opinions. Religious texts, horoscopes. Deadpan observations about others.","examples":["@pcelamed očito :)) Kronike iz Narnije su na rtl-u (obviously :)) Chronicles of Narnia is on RTL)","Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette. Žena gleda američki Masterchef. Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor. (Mom watches German Bachelorette. My wife watches American Masterchef. I'm starting to save for a third TV.)","Ne propustite večeras debatu kandidata za predsjednika @EU_Commission @hrtvijesti http://t.co/EgGMQ2dir7 (Don't miss tonight's debate of candidates for Commission president)"],"cues":"@reply + :), haha, sabor (parliament), debata (debate), dividenda (dividend), horoskop, numbers","not_for":"The poster's own annoyance or mishap, or bad news, go negative. Promotional or culture shares go positive."},"negative":{"what":"The poster complains, suffers a mishap, is annoyed, sad or worried, insults, mocks or moralises. Also news of bad things: crises, debt, conflicts, harsh criticism, accusations, lawsuits, deaths, mourning, scandals.","examples":["Naravno, opet kiša u Brusselsu. (Of course, rain in Brussels again.)","Putin na presici žestoko kritizira novo ukrajinsko vodstvo: 'Vojna akcija protiv Ukrajine će biti posljednja opcija!' (Putin harshly criticizes the new Ukrainian leadership)","@LucijaCavric oho i ovdje si finjak :P (oho, you're being posh here too)"],"cues":"opet (again), jebiga (damn it), mrzim (I hate), sranje (crap), grozan (awful), kritizira (criticizes), žalost (mourning), dug (debt), :(, :S","not_for":"Help appeals go positive. Witty observations about others and calm opinions go neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 9 scored 64.9, essentially the same as version 6 (65.1). The main remaining recoverable error is positive texts labelled neutral (45). Many are short friendly @replies or posts:
- invitations ('popit cemo kavu', 'kad idemo u kazalište?!');
- greetings ('dobar dan :)', 'pozdrav prijatelju');
- encouragement ('Bit će bolje, mora :)', 'zasluzeno');
- cheering ('ajmo Dinamo', 'Pričekaj Chelsea veceras').

Version 7 tried to rescue these with a broad 'friendly replies incl. playful laughter and agreement' rule. That pulled neutral banter into positive and lowered the score.

For the final version I keep version 9 and narrow the change: replies count as positive only when they contain a greeting, an invitation, encouragement or cheering. Laughter, agreement and informational replies with smileys stay neutral.

I drop 'fan chants' from neutral to avoid a conflict with cheering. I swap one positive example for an invitation reply and trim words to stay under 400. Everything else stays unchanged.","question":"What emotional attitude does the poster of this Croatian tweet convey, judged from its tone and from the valence of what it reports or shares?","rule":"Negative needs the poster to be bothered or attacking: their own complaint, mishap or suffering (even joked about), annoyance, sarcasm aimed at someone, moralising, or news of something bad (crisis, conflict, criticism, accusation, lawsuit, death, scandal). Conversational @replies, banter, deadpan observations, calm opinions, statistics, political or institutional events, religious texts and horoscopes are neutral; a smiley or laughter alone does not make a reply positive. Shares of culture, entertainment, tech, business deals, article teasers, tips, ads, check-ins, help appeals, and replies with warmth, greetings, invitations, encouragement or cheering are positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit joy, praise, thanks, love, excitement, greetings, invitations, encouragement, cheering. Shares of events, culture, celebrities, tech, business deals, article teasers, recipes and tips, ads and listings, check-ins, help appeals.","examples":["Pula: Na Giardinima započela 8. Florija, sajam cvijeća u sklopu obilježavanja Dana Grada: https://t.co/6Jbezcjeer (Pula: the 8th Florija flower fair started at Giardini)","Apartments Batur - Zadar - Croatia http://t.co/vLFrL36bKd http://t.co/05CLYU5jQL #croatia","RT @amaiia_hr: #Zagreb - Volonteri traže prijevoz do poplavljenih područja #poplave (Volunteers seek transport to flooded areas)","@Kjukar   Ako bude kakve srece, popit cemo kavu negdje ovih dana (If we're lucky, we'll have coffee one of these days)"],"cues":"festival, ponuda (offer), kako (how to), rekord (record), pročitajte (read), pomozimo (let's help), hvala (thanks), dobar dan (good day), ajmo (let's go), I'm at","not_for":"Smileys on complaints or digs go negative. @reply chat with only a smiley, laughter or plain information goes neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Casual @reply chat, banter, practical answers, plain questions. Statistics, dividends, line-ups. Political or institutional events and calm opinions. Religious texts, horoscopes. Deadpan observations about others.","examples":["@pcelamed očito :)) Kronike iz Narnije su na rtl-u (obviously :)) Chronicles of Narnia is on RTL)","Mama gleda njemačku Bachelorette. Žena gleda američki Masterchef. Počinjem štedjet za treći televizor. (Mom watches German Bachelorette. My wife watches American Masterchef. I'm starting to save for a third TV.)","Ne propustite večeras debatu kandidata za predsjednika @EU_Commission @hrtvijesti http://t.co/EgGMQ2dir7 (Don't miss tonight's debate of candidates for Commission president)"],"cues":"@reply + :), haha, sabor (parliament), debata (debate), dividenda (dividend), horoskop, numbers","not_for":"The poster's own annoyance or mishap, or bad news, go negative. Promotional or culture shares and greeting or cheering replies go positive."},"negative":{"what":"The poster complains, suffers a mishap, is annoyed, sad or worried, insults, mocks or moralises. Also news of bad things: crises, debt, conflicts, harsh criticism, accusations, lawsuits, deaths, mourning, scandals.","examples":["Naravno, opet kiša u Brusselsu. (Of course, rain in Brussels again.)","Putin na presici žestoko kritizira novo ukrajinsko vodstvo: 'Vojna akcija protiv Ukrajine će biti posljednja opcija!' (Putin harshly criticizes the new Ukrainian leadership)","@LucijaCavric oho i ovdje si finjak :P (oho, you're being posh here too)"],"cues":"opet (again), jebiga (damn it), mrzim (I hate), sranje (crap), grozan (awful), kritizira (criticizes), žalost (mourning), dug (debt), :(, :S","not_for":"Help appeals go positive. Witty observations about others and calm opinions go neutral."}}}
